                        "helpname": "loadmess",
                        "aliasOf": "loadmess",
                        "classname": "loadmess",
                        "operator": 0,
                        "versionId": -361086158,
                        "changesPatcherIO": 0
                    },
                    "text": "loadmess 200",
                    "varname": "ramp_ms"
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-36",
                    "linecount": 39,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 988.0, 522.0, 577.0, 582.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nselector_ramp_24 — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA stand-in for [selector~ 24 @ramptime <ms>], whose ramptime does not work in\nRNBO. 24 signal inlets, one signal outlet. Changing the selection crossfades\nlinearly from whatever is sounding now to the newly selected input over\nramp_ms. Selecting 0 fades everything out.\n\nA change made in the middle of a ramp starts a fresh ramp_ms crossfade from\nthe current mix, so rapid switching never jumps or clicks from a discontinuity.\nThe input gains always sum to 1 during a crossfade between inputs (linear, not\nequal-power: two uncorrelated inputs dip about 3 dB at the midpoint, the same\nas selector~/gate~ ramps).\n\nSource: utility, no paper. Models Max selector~ with @ramptime.\n\nIO (exception to the stereo IO contract: this is a mono router)\n  in1..in24: signal inputs 1..24\n  out1:      the selected input\n\nPARAMETERS (2)\n\n1. selection — 0…24 (integer), default 1\n   Which input is passed to the output. 0 = off (silence), like selector~.\n   Non-integer values are rounded. The first sample after load starts on this\n   input directly, with no fade-in.\n\n2. ramp_ms — 0…5000 ms, default 200 ms\n   Length of the linear crossfade after each selection change. 0 switches\n   instantly (one-sample step, like selector~ without ramptime). Exponential\n   taper (exponent 3) so the short, useful times get most of the slider.\n   Changing ramp_ms during a ramp changes the speed of the ramp in progress.\n\nNOTES\n- Unconnected inlets are silent, so patch only as many sources as you need.\n- CPU: 24 multiply-adds per sample when settled, plus a 24-gain update per\n  sample while a ramp is running.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
        ],
